  "conclusion": "Unconditional/adaptive bounds improve selected synthetic near-copy distributions but regress dense data; row gating reduces overhead but natural results lack consistent benefit. Four accumulator arrays show essentially no synthetic gain. Transposed scratch experiment is about1.32x baseline time on all synthetic groups and needs additional memory admission, so is not adopted. No production optimization or general whole-operation speedup claim.",
  "next_experiment": "A bounded exact f64 pair-distance cache could avoid second-pass recomputation. Any adoption requires explicit scratch admission, callback/error/bitwise-nearest equality and paired natural/whole-operation measurements. Float32 caching and approximate distances are not qualified by these results."
